 **Statement.** The record for one filesystem is the file `/var/lib/btrfs/scrub.status.<fsid>` (the base path plus a
-dot plus the filesystem UUID). Every update is written to a sibling file `scrub.status.<fsid>_tmp` and then moved
-over the record with `rename`, so a reader sees either the old or the new record, never a half-written one. A file
-the CLI creates gets mode 0600, and every open, for reading or writing, must take a non-blocking exclusive `flock`
-(`LOCK_EX`), so a second writer or a reader that finds the lock held fails at once instead of waiting.
